---
/*
 * Privacy.
 *
 * Written from what the code actually does rather than from a template. Every
 * processor listed below is one this site really sends data to — Supabase for
 * the database, payOS for the transfer, Vercel for the hosting, Resend for the
 * one email form, Google for the fonts and the pattern generator's model.
 *
 * If a service is added or dropped, this list is the thing to change. A privacy
 * page that lists processors the site no longer uses is worse than none: it
 * reads as boilerplate and stops being believed.
 */
import PolicyPage from '../components/PolicyPage.astro';
import { RETURNS_WINDOW_DAYS, SHOP_ADDRESS, SHOP_EMAIL } from '../lib/shop';

const processors = [
  {
    name: 'Supabase',
    role: 'Stores the shop database — the catalogue and your order.',
    where: 'Hosted database',
  },
  {
    name: 'payOS',
    role: 'Takes the bank transfer. Receives your name, email and the amount.',
    where: 'Vietnam',
  },
  {
    name: 'Vercel',
    role: 'Hosts and serves this site, and keeps short-lived request logs.',
    where: 'Global CDN',
  },
  {
    name: 'Resend',
    role: 'Delivers the email from the product-request form.',
    where: 'Email delivery',
  },
  {
    name: 'Google Fonts',
    role: 'Serves the typefaces. Your browser fetches these directly.',
    where: 'Global CDN',
  },
  {
    name: 'Google Gemini',
    role: 'Generates images in the pattern generator, from the prompt you type.',
    where: 'AI model API',
  },
  {
    name: 'Your courier',
    role: 'Receives your name, address and phone number so the parcel can arrive.',
    where: 'Varies by destination',
  },
];
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Your details"
  description="What this shop collects, why it needs it, who else sees it, and how long it is kept."
  intro="A small shop needs surprisingly little about you. Here is all of it, why each piece is needed, and everywhere it goes."
  updated="2026-08-28"
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version.</strong> There are no accounts, no advertising trackers and no
      analytics on this site. Your details are collected to send you a parcel, and that is what they
      are used for.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What is collected, and why</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>What</th>
        <th>Why it is needed</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Name</td>
        <td>To address the parcel and to know who I am talking to.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Email address</td>
        <td>
          To confirm the order and to answer you. It is also half the key to your order tracking.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Phone number</td>
        <td>Couriers here will not attempt a delivery without one.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Delivery address</td>
        <td>To get the parcel to the right door.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>What you ordered, and what you paid</td>
        <td>To pack it, to account for it, and to handle a return later.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Anything you type in the note box</td>
        <td>Because you asked me to read it.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>A bank reference from payOS</td>
        <td>To match your transfer to your order. No card or account number reaches this site.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Your basket lives in your own browser's local storage until you check out. It is not sent
    anywhere until you ask for a price or place an order, and clearing your browser data clears it.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not collected</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No card or bank details.</strong> Payment happens entirely inside payOS and your own
      banking app. This site never sees them and could not store them if it wanted to.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No accounts and no passwords.</strong> There is nothing to sign up for.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>No analytics, advertising pixels or third-party trackers.</strong> Nothing here follows
      you to another site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No marketing emails.</strong> Your address is not added to a list, because there is no
      list.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>

  <p>
    One, and only for me: signing in to the back office sets a session cookie so the admin pages stay
    unlocked for a day. Shoppers are never issued a cookie. That is why there is no cookie banner —
    there is nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees your details</h2>

  <p>
    Only the services that have to, and only the part each one needs. Nothing is ever sold, rented or
    handed to anyone for marketing.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Service</th>
        <th>What it does</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        processors.map((p) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <strong>{p.name}</strong>
              <br />
              <span style="font-size:0.8125rem;opacity:0.7">{p.where}</span>
            </td>
            <td>{p.role}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Because these services operate internationally, your details may be processed outside your own
    country. There is no way to run an online shop otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>The pattern generator</h2>

  <p>
    Prompts typed into the pattern generator are sent to Google's Gemini API to produce an image. Do
    not type anything into it you would not want leaving this site. Prompts are not stored in the
    shop database.
  </p>

  <h2>How long things are kept</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Orders</strong> — kept while they are useful for accounting and for handling a return
      or a query, which is well beyond the {RETURNS_WINDOW_DAYS}-day returns window.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Abandoned checkouts</strong> — an order that is never paid for is cancelled
      automatically once its payment window closes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Emails you send me</strong> — kept as long as the conversation is useful, then deleted.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you can ask for</h2>

  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SHOP_EMAIL}`}>{SHOP_EMAIL}</a> and I will:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Tell you everything held about you, and send you a copy.</li>
    <li>Correct anything wrong — a mistyped address, a changed name.</li>
    <li>
      Delete it, once nothing outstanding depends on it. Records tied to a completed sale may need to
      be kept for accounting.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This is one person reading that inbox rather than a department, so expect a human reply within a
    few days.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>

  <p>
    ZippyZack, {SHOP_ADDRESS.join(', ')}. Questions about any of this go to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SHOP_EMAIL}`}>{SHOP_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    If this page changes in a way that affects what happens to details already collected, the date
    below changes with it.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
